# Real user/analysis data lives in the local app.db and, from 86bbwachy
# onward, in per-run artifact files (raw prompts/responses/context) under
# runs_dir (default var/runs/, see docs/technical/run-instrumentation.md
# §5.2). *.db/*.sqlite catches the former; var/ catches the latter, added
# proactively here BEFORE that directory exists, not after something first
# lands in it. Neither is a secret in the API-key sense, but both are this
# project's own real data and stay local-only, same posture as _audit/ below.
# `.gitignore` only stops NEW files from being tracked -- confirmed live
# 2026-09-24 that this doesn't retroactively apply to something already
# committed: src/app.db (a stale, harmless FastAPI-tutorial-scaffold test DB
# from project init, checked directly -- no real data) had been tracked since
# 2026-04-06 despite *.db being long in place. Untracked and deleted; if a
# new .db/var/ path ever needs tracking for a legitimate reason, that's a
# deliberate `git add -f`, not an accident.
*.db
*.sqlite
var/

# 2026-09 prompt audit rigs, caches and logs. Reference material, never shipped.
# See _audit/README.md. Kept out of git deliberately: throwaway measurement
# scaffolding, live provider data in the caches, and ~40MB of run logs.
_audit/
